<#
  Fix-SlowNetworkAndJobFlow.ps1
  Compatible with Windows PowerShell 5.1 (no PS7-only syntax used).

  What this fixes:

  1. SLOW-CONNECTION GPS ("harder to find rider locations / vendor's
     current location on slow internet")
     src\utils\geolocation.js used a flat 15s timeout for getReliableLocation()
     regardless of connection speed. Most phones use Assisted-GPS, which
     downloads a small ephemeris/almanac file over the network to speed up
     the very first fix - on weak Kano mobile signal that download alone can
     take 15-20+ seconds, so the old timeout was cutting off a GPS fix that
     was actually still working, just waiting on the network. Now detects a
     slow/constrained connection (2G/slow-2G/3G/save-data via the Network
     Information API) and extends both the per-fix and overall timeout
     windows, with clearer "slow connection detected" progress messaging.
     src\components\rider\DriverHeartbeat.jsx shares the same connection
     helper and gets the same widened per-fix timeout for its continuous
     location pings.

  2. BID ACCEPTANCE -> IMMEDIATE ASSIGNMENT
     Checked the DB layer directly (Supabase): accept_bid() and
     accept_order_direct() already atomically assign the order and flip the
     rider to 'busy' the instant a bid/base-price is accepted - that part
     was already correct. The actual gap was on the rider's screen: when a
     VENDOR accepted a rider's counter-offer bid, the rider was never told -
     their bid just silently disappeared from the dashboard with no
     notification or redirect, even though the job was already theirs
     server-side. Now the rider dashboard's realtime bid listener detects an
     accepted bid and immediately shows a confirmation and redirects
     straight into /rider/active-job.

  3. RIDER MUST STAY ONLINE UNTIL THE JOB IS DONE
     Found two related bugs in src\app\rider\(main)\dashboard\page.jsx and
     active-job\page.jsx:
       a) A rider could navigate back to the dashboard mid-job (nav bar,
          browser back) and tap "Go Offline" - or a mislabeled "Go Online"
          button that would silently overwrite their 'busy' status back to
          'online' mid-delivery. The dashboard now checks for an
          in-progress order (matched/picked_up/in_transit) on load and
          immediately redirects to the active job instead of showing the
          feed/toggle at all, with a defensive block inside the toggle
          itself as a second line of defense against races.
       b) Nothing ever reversed the 'busy' operational_status the accept
          RPCs set when a job starts - a rider who completed their very
          first delivery stayed permanently invisible to the dispatch
          engine (which only looks at operational_status = 'online') and
          stuck showing "offline" on their own heartbeat forever after.
          active-job/page.jsx now flips the rider back to 'online' the
          moment a delivery is marked delivered.

  4. PICKUP SLIDER GATED TO THE PICKUP LOCATION (only that step)
     src\components\rider\SlideToConfirm.jsx is a generic, location-blind
     slider reused for every stage - a rider could previously slide to
     "picked up" from anywhere in town. active-job/page.jsx now runs a
     lightweight live GPS watch while heading to pickup and only unlocks
     the "Slide to confirm Pickup" step once the rider is within ~400m of
     the pickup point (deliberately generous - "general location", not an
     exact building, given Kano's informal addressing). The "Slide to start
     Transit" and "Slide to Mark Delivered" steps are untouched, exactly as
     you asked. If GPS genuinely fails, it falls back to an unlocked slider
     with a warning rather than permanently blocking a rider's income.

  5. SHARE LINK GETS A REAL PREVIEW IMAGE ("site image" feature)
     The tracking link (/tracking/[orderId]) had no per-order metadata at
     all, so sharing it on WhatsApp/SMS fell back to the generic homepage
     branding image with no indication of which delivery it was. Added:
       - src\app\tracking\[orderId]\opengraph-image.jsx: a dynamically
         generated preview card (Next.js's built-in file convention, wired
         up automatically) showing status + pickup -> drop-off route,
         reusing the same "safe fields only" rule as the public tracking
         API (never price, phone numbers, or account identity).
       - src\app\tracking\[orderId]\layout.jsx: per-order title/description
         metadata (status-aware, e.g. "Rider assigned - NaijaDrops").

  This script writes full file content (base64-encoded, written as raw
  bytes - no PowerShell string-escaping of JS/JSX template literals, no
  BOM-injection risk from Set-Content -Encoding UTF8). Backs up every
  existing file it touches to .fix-backup-slownetwork-jobflow\ first.

  Run from the ROOT of your local repo clone:
      powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\Fix-SlowNetworkAndJobFlow.ps1
#>

$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"
$root = Get-Location
$backupDir = Join-Path $root ".fix-backup-slownetwork-jobflow"
if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $backupDir)) { New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $backupDir | Out-Null }

if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $root "src\app"))) {
    Write-Host "ERROR: src\app not found. Run this script from the repo root." -ForegroundColor Red
    exit 1
}

function Get-FullPath($rel) { return Join-Path $root $rel }

function Backup-Path($full) {
    if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $full) {
        $rel = $full.Substring($root.Path.Length).TrimStart('\','/')
        $dest = Join-Path $backupDir $rel
        $destParent = Split-Path $dest -Parent
        if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $destParent)) { New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $destParent -Force | Out-Null }
        Copy-Item -LiteralPath $full -Destination $dest -Force
    }
}

# Writes exact raw bytes decoded from base64 - sidesteps every PowerShell
# 5.1 string-encoding gotcha (BOM injection, backtick/`$`/quote escaping in
# JS template literals) entirely, since we never construct the file content
# as a PowerShell string at all.
function Write-FileFromBase64($relPath, $b64) {
    $full = Get-FullPath $relPath
    $targetParent = Split-Path $full -Parent
    if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $targetParent)) { New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $targetParent -Force | Out-Null }
    Backup-Path $full
    $bytes = [Convert]::FromBase64String($b64)
    [System.IO.File]::WriteAllBytes($full, $bytes)
    Write-Host "  WROTE: $relPath" -ForegroundColor Green
}

Write-Host "`nApplying slow-network GPS, job-assignment, stay-online, pickup-geofence, and share-preview fixes:" -ForegroundColor Cyan

$b64_GEOLOCATION = ""
Write-FileFromBase64 "src\utils\geolocation.js" $b64_GEOLOCATION

$b64_HEARTBEAT = ""
Write-FileFromBase64 "src\components\rider\DriverHeartbeat.jsx" $b64_HEARTBEAT

$b64_DASHBOARD = ""
Write-FileFromBase64 "src\app\rider\(main)\dashboard\page.jsx" $b64_DASHBOARD

$b64_ACTIVEJOB = ""
Write-FileFromBase64 "src\app\rider\(main)\active-job\page.jsx" $b64_ACTIVEJOB

$b64_OGIMAGE = ""
Write-FileFromBase64 "src\app\tracking\[orderId]\opengraph-image.jsx" $b64_OGIMAGE

$b64_TRACKLAYOUT = ""
Write-FileFromBase64 "src\app\tracking\[orderId]\layout.jsx" $b64_TRACKLAYOUT

Write-Host "`nDone. Backups of any pre-existing files saved under .fix-backup-slownetwork-jobflow\" -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host "Next: npm run build (or your usual dev command), then redeploy to Vercel." -ForegroundColor Cyan
